description:
cohesion.lcom finds the SAME defect in five classes, not five coincidences: a class that both MEASURES (needs a GPU, a corpus, or the published predictions) and RENDERS (needs only the dicts the measurement produced) reads as disconnected method clusters and its table cannot be exercised without constructing the measuring apparatus.

Five landed already on this shape: AttributionReport, StackCoverageReport, SlotTiesReport, TieDivergenceReport, CropLateralityReport. Three carry the same {report} island and are not yet split:
  ServeBench       kneemri/inference/serve_bench.py   LCOM4 3, islands {pixels,synchronise,timed} {graphs} {report}
  OutOfFoldOracle  kneemri/evaluation/oof_oracle.py   LCOM4 3, islands {covariates} {routing} {report}
  ReaderAgreement  kneemri/labels/reader_agreement.py LCOM4 3, islands {_resample,by_label,gap,report} {error_report,errors} {cells}

ReaderAgreement is the one that needs thought rather than a move: its report is NOT a pure island, it shares _resample with the measurement, so the split is a judgement call about which side the resampling belongs on.

NOT in scope: TrainingOptions (LCOM4 5). A config dataclass with disjoint accessor clusters is what a config IS - splitting it would be churn.

Each split is: move the render half to a frozen dataclass beside its producer, fields = exactly what the render reads, method renamed to lines(); update main() and the mirror test (the method-level mirror gate wants test_lines). Regenerate archmap in the SAME commit.
